<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Pre-raid Best in Slot Gear list for Unholy Death Knight DPS in Cataclysm Classic Phase 1. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Heroic Dungeons, reputations and professions.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c6">Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear for Unholy Death Knight DPS in Phase 1</span></h2>
<a class="icontiny c6" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=6/death-knight">
<img alt="Death Knight" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_deathknight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Knight</span></a>s will need to reach the <i>hit cap</i> which effects our abilites in Cataclysm Classic. Due to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=61455/runic-focus">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_hand_09.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Runic Focus</span></a> we do not need to worry about spell-hit cap, as we also reach that along with our melee hit cap.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Hit Rating - You will want a total of <i>at least</i> +8% chance to hit. This means you'll want at least 961 hit rating in total. There are no longer any buffs or debuffs from your raid to influence your hit rating, so you need to make sure you're sorted from gear.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Expertise Rating - Expertise is a mediocre stat for <a class="icontiny c6" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=6/death-knight">
<img alt="Death Knight" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_deathknight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Knight</span></a>s. It reduces the chance that your and auto attacks, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=55090/scourge-strike">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_scourgestrike.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Scourge Strike</span></a>  and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=85948/festering-strike">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_61.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Festering Strike</span></a> will be dodged or parried. When they do, you get you runes refunded, meaning the penalty is very small.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Strength - Strength is the primary base stat for <a class="icontiny c6" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=6/death-knight">
<img alt="Death Knight" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_deathknight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death Knight</span></a>s, and is always good to get more of. It gives 2 attack power per point, before modifiers are applied.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Attack Power, Critical Strike Rating, Mastery Rating, and Haste Rating all blend together as stats that are desireable, but with lower value than Strength.</div></li></ol>
